      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": true,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>As long as you are in melee range, regardless of whether or not the dice make range (maybe due to elevation), the push would occur at the end of the attack. That&#39;s how I&#39;ve played it. However, the rulebook says that Push attacks &quot;move a target hit by this attack that number of hexes&quot;, so it&#39;s very possible that the Push is dependant on damage taken if you read this literally.</p><p>I believe that Push is mandatory. It does not say &quot;up to&quot; and the glossary says it&#39;s a &quot;forced&quot; movement &quot;that number of hexes&quot;.&nbsp;</p><p>Maybe Paul will chime in on this. I&#39;d be interested in his answer.</p>",
