    {
      "id": 124804,
      "name": "Paul",
      "username": "Paul",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/paul/{size}/5862_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-04-08T14:54:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p><span><strong>Official Rule Time!</strong></span></p><p>1) Push is not optional, and must be the number specified in the ability; i.e., \"Push 3\" must always Push the target 3 hexes, not 1 or 2. However, as Humble-Knight mentioned, you can make any Push beyond 1 end on the original space if you move people the right way.</p><p>2) Push is separate from damage. If Proletariat attacks a target and deals no damage, that target is still Pushed.</p><p>3) Characters are immune to the effects of their attacks. This includes damage, which is the most common case, as well as effects like Push. TL;DR - Proletariat cannot Push Proletariat.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:58:53.848Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 11772,
      "topic_slug": "proletariats-push",
      "display_username": "Paul",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "Judges",
      "flair_url": "scale-balanced",
      "flair_bg_color": "7700ff",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 42,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": true,
      "user_title": "Chief Justice",
      "title_is_group": false,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Official Rule Time!</strong></span></p><p>1) Push is not optional, and must be the number specified in the ability; i.e., \"Push 3\" must always Push the target 3 hexes, not 1 or 2. However, as Humble-Knight mentioned, you can make any Push beyond 1 end on the original space if you move people the right way.</p><p>2) Push is separate from damage. If Proletariat attacks a target and deals no damage, that target is still Pushed.</p><p>3) Characters are immune to the effects of their attacks. This includes damage, which is the most common case, as well as effects like Push. TL;DR - Proletariat cannot Push Proletariat.</p>",
